# Testing Guidelines

## TDD Cycle
Red → Green → Refactor (required for new backend domain/application logic).

## Testing Pyramid
1. Unit (domain, value objects, specifications)
2. Integration (repositories, use cases with test DB when applicable)
3. Contract / E2E (when present)

## Coverage Targets (backend)
- Domain: 95%
- Application: 90%
- Infrastructure: 70%
- Global API: 80%

## Test location & naming
- Backend: `*.spec.ts` colocated with source (`apps/api`)
- Naming: `Given_When_Then` or descriptive `describe/it`
- Example: `GivenActiveStudent_WhenScheduleClass_ThenClassIsCreated`

## What must be tested
- Business rules, edge cases, domain events, authorization, validation

## When to add app tests
- Add or update tests when changing non-trivial logic in `apps/app` hooks, utils, or mappers — not for purely visual tweaks

## Forbidden
- Flaky tests, sleep-based sync, shared mutable test state

## Before commit (when user requests commit)
Run relevant tests: `cd apps/api && npm test` (and app tests if touched).
